  "body": "\"While a user agent is running the above algorithm for an element x, there must be a strong reference from the element's node document to the element x, even if that element is not in its Document.\"\n\nThis appears directly under an algorithm detailing how to dispatch a progress event. Presumably it should be placed a little higher, under \"update the image data\"? We should also update the statement to \"in a shadow-including document\".\n\n(A couple of subsections might also help out with the general description of the `<img>` element. It appears rather unorganized.)\n",
